# Two scopes sharing a state-bearing output variable name (WF-020 guard)

Labeled variable states lower to plain internal attributes whose `#` is
mangled to a space (`heffing#bruto` → `heffing bruto`). A rule name that
recurs across scopes is qualified by subject so it stays globally unique
(WF-020). Both scopes below declare the SAME state-bearing output variable
`heffing`, so their step rules (`berekening heffing bruto`, `berekening
heffing netto`) would collide unless the cross-scope ambiguity is detected on
the mangled name — the detector (`ruled_vnames_of`) mangles exactly as the
rule labeller does. Own-authored, rights-free.

```catala
declaration scope Eerste:
  input grondslag content integer
  output heffing content integer
    state bruto
    state netto

declaration scope Tweede:
  input grondslag content integer
  output heffing content integer
    state bruto
    state netto

scope Eerste:
  definition heffing state bruto equals grondslag
  definition heffing state netto equals heffing - 10

scope Tweede:
  definition heffing state bruto equals grondslag
  definition heffing state netto equals heffing - 20
```
